{\\mathrm{d}x}=4,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|4 x|=4|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{4}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{4}{|4 x|\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 4\\int \\frac{1}{|4 x|\\sqrt{(4 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 4(\\frac{1}{4})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 1\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(4 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|4 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676960 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "142408c4-a856-5ba3-9cb3-fdd989d60438" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676886} {:answer/id #uuid "1d9079dc-e0e9-5883-9ee0-be4e84800886" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676892} {:answer/id #uuid "4b039ee6-7d56-5a1f-923a-48cd9541fb4e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676923} {:answer/id #uuid "c69ee190-e333-5892-a21c-1640d2670d8a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}}{3}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677006} {:answer/id #uuid "e88d8113-27e3-54e9-aa5a-f4c0374e5bd7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(9 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677024}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676892} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0a36f36-3cca-5caf-af0f-d26099a43110" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677016}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "84c7e966-96b7-5e2c-ab4c-0d93d8c57026" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=3 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=3,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|3 x|=3|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{3}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{3}{|x|\\sqrt{9 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9\\int \\frac{1}{|3 x|\\sqrt{(3 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9(\\frac{1}{3})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 3\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 3 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= 3 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|3 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676964 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "30aa92c4-ebd0-55bf-9c66-85ea2a24fa20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "13 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(13 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676906} {:answer/id #uuid "3a65b91e-5c21-5e2c-b3c6-a218b18b9bad" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(13 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186