rcsec}{\\left(13 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|13 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676965 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0f28e42b-8620-5ae1-8f04-805f88867c6c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "8 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676881} {:answer/id #uuid "228bf48b-6c00-5de6-bd83-cd4703885c3b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676897} {:answer/id #uuid "75d06d6f-6fe5-5d6f-9007-78758ffc948c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676947} {:answer/id #uuid "bc16c7b4-f2db-5f7c-a2ff-83546ce380d9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676998} {:answer/id #uuid "f3779970-0bfa-5296-b548-2b234032333d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676897} :answer-field/id #uuid "77b14ff6-ee23-5c1a-82b3-746ee344c414" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676950}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8ec467ed-a842-5743-90ea-dc3e43a5c825" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{8}{|2 x|\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=2 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{2})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|2 x|=2|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{2}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{8}{|2 x|\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 8\\int \\frac{1}{|2 x|\\sqrt{(2 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 8(\\frac{1}{2})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 4\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= 4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(2 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|2 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4062c6f4-8073-59e2-8572-082fb67e86cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(3 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676918} {:answer/id #uuid "54a15aad-5ed5-5e4d-ba7e-1c0422c019cd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676929} {:answer/id #uuid "95e14540-a907-57a9-af56-5c13e9653546" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{3} \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676970} {:answer/id #uuid "d6b5ffaf-8545-5b67-a43e-b06901fddd7e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "3 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677014} {:answer/id #uuid "f03be629-e361-57e1-aa79-d89c4c2e71ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677027}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677027} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c2ce00a-b685-5520-b2c9-cc2b514b71f2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676953}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486} :question/id #uuid "9109a0e2-f715-5496-8bcd-2bf0c487318b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{3 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=\\sqrt{3} x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=\\sqrt{3},\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|\\sqrt{3} x|=\\sqrt{3}|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{9}{|x|\\sqrt{3 x^{2} - 1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9 \\sqrt{3}\\int \\frac{1}{|\\sqrt{3} x|\\sqrt{(\\sqrt{3} x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 9 \\sqrt{3}(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 9\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= 9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{3} x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|\\sqrt{3} x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13b0f660-67ce-59a2-9cf2-d36d0c375fff" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(10 x \\right)}}{100}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676885} {:answer/id #uuid "1d12d78c-c5a9-5229-adea-c3244ab0d11f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(10 x \\right)}}{10}+C" :db/id