\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|\\sqrt{7} x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677001 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e3c92a4-a7da-51b0-8625-d966303b5bd9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "20 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(5 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676893} {:answer/id #uuid "ba9ea4eb-0793-5e14-bb35-81349da6a845" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(5 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676994} {:answer/id #uuid "c566ac9c-ddcc-5843-b570-313dfc0d0833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(5 x \\right)}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677005} {:answer/id #uuid "e626e4b2-798b-511a-9112-b64176edcf02" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677019} {:answer/id #uuid "fab2d188-b643-5b6e-a5ee-efa3c8f819df" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "4 \\operatorname{arctan}{\\left(5 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677038}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676994} :answer-field/id #uuid "d6e53eea-4a9c-579c-9473-40e52033ceba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677015}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "c2cb4fba-879b-5b01-9945-6bb60bed682b" :question/problem "Evaluate the integral. Give an exact answer.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{20}{|5 x|\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$" :question/retired true :question/worked-solution "Use the linear substitution $u=5 x.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5,\\qquad \\mathrm{d}x=(\\frac{1}{5})\\,\\mathrm{d}u.\n$$\n\nThe substitution factor is positive, so the absolute values satisfy\n\n$$\n|u|=|5 x|=5|x|,\\qquad \\frac{1}{|x|}=\\frac{5}{|u|}.\n$$\n\nApply the basic inverse-trigonometric integral:\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}& \\int \\frac{20}{|5 x|\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 20\\int \\frac{1}{|5 x|\\sqrt{(5 x)^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\  &= 20(\\frac{1}{5})\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 4\\int \\frac{1}{|u|\\sqrt{u^{2}-1}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u \\\\  &= 4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(u \\right)}+C \\\\  &= 4 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(5 x \\right)}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis antiderivative applies on either interval where $|5 x|>1$; the constant may differ between those intervals."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186677008 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "040ea9c9-e715-507d-902d-bb71351804ed" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{7} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676876} {:answer/id #uuid "335a8d6a-b4ec-5193-a45f-51bf7646df64" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\sqrt{7} \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{7} x \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676908} {:answer/id #uuid "6ec7ce1f-0eb4-59d3-a1a0-ac1e9f4398a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\sqrt{7} \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{7} x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186676943} {:answer/id #uuid "e645444e-55cd-5743-bd4c-ad58f4b945a5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(\\sqrt{7} x \\right)}}{7}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677020} {:answer/id #uuid "f88a3601-88ce-58e0-8eaa-5fa3af7b4c28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "9 \\operatorname{arcsec}{\\left(7 x \\right)}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186677034}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186676876} :answer-field/id #uuid "